  "description": "10/192026 Update… stock arriving by November, stay tuned!\nThe Kissena is the namesake of NYC’s home track. Built in 1964 as part of the world’s fair, “the track of dreams” is our beautiful, gritty, four corner asphalt playground. True to form, our homage is a hardcore aluminum race bike created to carry the legacy of New York City’s mecca for track cycling the Kissena Velodrome.\nThe Kissena is also one of the most proven aluminum track frame sets in the market with UCI track world championships earning Affinity the honor of rainbow stripes. Additionally, we’ve earned over 20 US stars and stripes track national championships, European six-day victories and many Red Hook Crit wins… plus it’s a beast on the streets.\nOur latest revision includes a tapered head tube, a 43mm track specific fork allows up to 140mm stem for aero gains, lower stand over creates more seat mast… plus a head set is included!\nConstructed of 7005 aircraft grade aluminum tubing, proprietary geometry, and an integrated seat mast provide unmatched strength and stability. Beefy rear drop outs with replaceable inserts prevent slipping, and our short rear triangle with a seat tube cut out makes for a tight wheel base and aero tucked away wheel position.\nKey Features:\n• Crimson Sparkle/khaki graphics… satin finish\n• Proprietary track specific carbon fork\n• Integrated seat mast with cut out\n• 27.2 Wedge clamp\n• World Championship design",
